(7732374, 1273936, 114285, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by LevT:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Neat:</b></div><hr/><i> Going back commenting on images Ive already voted on. This is really a neat shot, pity the colours are a little bit flat, in the sky and the water. Nevertheless amazing capture.<br/> <br/>LevT?? I think so. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>"...a Neat shot" )). Thank you Anita, it''s the best compliment coming from you, and you are as prescient as ever in identifying the author. I could pump up the colors of course, but decided it would look better this, more natural way. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Haha thanks. I only dream of taking a shot like this one day, a thrilling moment indeed!<br/>Congrats on your ribbon.</td>', 'Originally posted by LevT: Originally posted by Neat: Going back commenting on images Ive already voted on. This is really a neat shot, pity the colours are a little bit flat, in the sky and the water. Nevertheless amazing capture. LevT?? I think so.  "...a Neat shot" )). Thank you Anita, it''s the best compliment coming from you, and you are as prescient as ever in identifying the author. I could pump up the colors of course, but decided it would look better this, more natural way.   Haha thanks. I only dream of taking a shot like this one day, a thrilling moment indeed!Congrats on your ribbon.', '2022-11-08 22:58:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(7732382, 1273837, 63398, '<td valign="top">Good on you!<br/> <br/>First, terrific image.<br/> <br/>Second, you''d best bring a box of Kleenex for your cop.<br/> <br/>Nothing is harder than to watch your dog die before he should.<br/> <br/>A dog is part of your life.<br/> <br/>You are his/her whole life.<br/> <br/>He will be overcome by your gift.<br/> <br/>Sometimes, this photography stuff is an arrow to the heart.</td>', 'Good on you! First, terrific image. Second, you''d best bring a box of Kleenex for your cop. Nothing is harder than to watch your dog die before he should. A dog is part of your life. You are his/her whole life. He will be overcome by your gift. Sometimes, this photography stuff is an arrow to the heart.', '2022-11-09 00:33:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(7732495, 1273994, 38162, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by glad2badad:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by oldbimmercoupe:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by glad2badad:</b></div><hr/><i> I find this a bit disturbing as an image to be entered here on DPC.  Perhaps that''s your intent (the shock factor)? </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Really?  Wow.  Now that says volumes. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>In what regard?  I thought the display of the man on the right with his private parts covered as they were, seemed a bit over the top and somewhat disgusting for public viewing.<br/> <br/>Would love to hear your thoughts on your follow-up comment. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Why try to explain after you have verbalized in clear terms an intolerance towards photography that doesnt meet your very ridged definition of art and freedom of expression (by the artist and the subjects apparently). No wonder DPC is barely a shadow of its former self. So we are left with bugs and puppies so the very few can act all self important and chummy. Cancel culture at the extreme.  Hope nothing offends you going forward.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by glad2badad - fixed quote attribute to correct person.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by glad2badad: Originally posted by oldbimmercoupe: Originally posted by glad2badad: I find this a bit disturbing as an image to be entered here on DPC.  Perhaps that''s your intent (the shock factor)?  Really?  Wow.  Now that says volumes.  In what regard?  I thought the display of the man on the right with his private parts covered as they were, seemed a bit over the top and somewhat disgusting for public viewing. Would love to hear your thoughts on your follow-up comment.   Why try to explain after you have verbalized in clear terms an intolerance towards photography that doesnt meet your very ridged definition of art and freedom of expression (by the artist and the subjects apparently). No wonder DPC is barely a shadow of its former self. So we are left with bugs and puppies so the very few can act all self important and chummy. Cancel culture at the extreme.  Hope nothing offends you going forward.Message edited by glad2badad - fixed quote attribute to correct person.', '2022-11-10 10:38:27.000000', NULL, 0),
